{
    "_comment": "Ours, with the per-transform retain_stats replaced by the pipeline-level statistics bracket. The snapshot runs after the geometry and the restore before the trailing crop and normalization: each batch draws two of mean/std/p1/p99 per channel and solves for the affine map that puts those two back, with the std and the two percentile targets scaled by a factor drawn from [0.9, 1.1] so the profile the network sees is never exactly the one the patch arrived with. Every transform's own retain_stats is false here: the two mechanisms do not compose, and the pipeline-level one is the point of this config. Derived from transform_params_one-sequence-to-segment-them-all.json, which is unchanged.",
